; Confirms the NOEL-V naive-WCET base-admission result on real hardware,
; recomputed with aberr removed from the analysis entirely (it's dispatched
; on-demand, not as a periodic rate-group member -- see aberr_load.seq).
; 3/6 remaining tasks are simultaneously schedulable under naive (all-miss)
; WCET with m=2 workers: startracker, kalman, low_pass_filter -- proven
; optimal (0.00% gap) with zero extra copies fitting on top even once
; aberr is out of the picture. Balanced per-task bucket assignment (each
; task at its own tightest-fitting rate group).
;
; Default (mutex-protected) BPFPrimeTest binary. All three tasks here are in
; the same 1Hz group and startracker/low_pass_filter share map fd2,
; kalman/low_pass_filter share fd4 -- with the shared-worker-pool
; architecture (not per-bucket isolated), the scheduler can dispatch any two
; of them to different cores at overlapping times. The default binary's
; shared_mutex serializes that access (no memory corruption, just
; non-deterministic ordering); use the BPF_MAPS_ALLOW_RACES build to
; observe the race unprotected.

; ---- Map setup ----

; Startracker: fd0, fd1, fd2
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.BPF_MAP_CREATE 0, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY, 4, 4, 7, 0
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.tests.POPULATE_MAP_RANDOM, 0, 0, 7
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.BPF_MAP_CREATE 1, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY, 4, 4, 7, 0
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.tests.POPULATE_MAP_RANDOM, 1, 0, 7
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.BPF_MAP_CREATE 2, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY, 4, 4, 7, 0
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.tests.POPULATE_MAP_RANDOM, 2, 0, 7

; Kalman: fd3, fd4
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.BPF_MAP_CREATE 3, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY, 4, 4, 7, 0
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.tests.POPULATE_MAP_RANDOM, 3, 0, 7
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.BPF_MAP_CREATE 4, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY, 4, 4, 7, 0
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.tests.POPULATE_MAP_RANDOM, 4, 0, 7

; low_pass_filter's compiled program hardcodes in_map=fd2 (shared with
; startracker), out_map=fd4 (shared with kalman) -- both already created above.

; ---- Load one VM instance per program ----

R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.LOAD_SEQUENCE 0, "tests/startracker/a.o"
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.LOAD_SEQUENCE 1, "tests/kalman/a.o"
R00:00:01 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.LOAD_SEQUENCE 2, "tests/low_pass_filter/a.o"

; ---- Start the rate groups (1s buffer after loads) ----

; 1Hz: startracker (64.2% naive), kalman (40.4% naive), low_pass_filter (39.5% naive)
R00:00:02 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.SetVMRateGroup 0, 1.0, 641.54
R00:00:02 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.SetVMRateGroup 1, 1.0, 403.70
R00:00:02 BPFPrimeTest.bpfSequencer.SetVMRateGroup 2, 1.0, 394.66

; Watch for: zero SchedulerSlip events on vm 0-2 over an extended run.
